  m_Name: Object_43
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Right Front Sensor
  description: The Right Front Sensor is a tiny, complex-shaped component located
    at the bottom-right-front of the engine, made of Material.001, which monitors
    various engine parameters, such as temperature, pressure, or flow rates, providing
    crucial data to the engine control unit, enabling it to optimize engine performance,
    efficiency, and emissions, and its compact design allows for unobtrusive installation.
    The sensor's front position exposes it to the engine's intake system, making
    it susceptible to contamination from airborne particles. One interesting aspect
    of this sensor is its ability to detect even slight deviations in engine performance,
    allowing for prompt corrective action.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
